46. Core Principle

The central principle of the AI-DOS is:

An AI should not be evaluated solely by what it can do or what it outputs, but by what it is operationally specified and authorized to do, under what information and environmental conditions, with which entities it is coupled, and what configuration trajectory its actions may produce.

⸻

47. Operational Principle

A concise operational form is:

Before Action:

Identify → Verify → Authorize → Constrain → Act

After Action:

Observe → Evaluate → Update → Reassess

Therefore:

AI Safety Operation = Pre-action Configuration Assessment + Controlled Action + Post-action Configuration Assessment

